//? Title: Karatsuba multiplication: inspect the three actual products
//? Subtitle: Decimal carry, the crossover32 base case and measured recursive work
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Karatsuba replaces four half-products by three, but a practical implementation
still uses schoolbook leaves. We start just above the native crossover, retain
the original31-digit constants, and inspect actual recursive call roles, operand
widths and result lengths. The original constants themselves use a schoolbook
leaf, so theoretical power curves alone cannot describe that run. Native
counters separate digit multiplications from omitted digit operations,
allocations and timing.
)

\toc

> Start just beyond the actual crossover

The implementation uses a schoolbook leaf whenever either operand has at most32
digits. Two33-digit all-nine values therefore give a genuine first split. The
diagram uses the producing invocation records, with actual low/high/sum children
and their digit widths. Recursive low slices can retain high zero positions;
recorded widths describe actual vectors rather than inferred magnitudes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/karatsuba_split.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/karatsuba.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <limits>
#include <cmath>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto t =
        dm::algorithms::karatsuba_trace(std::string(33, '9'),
                                        std::string(33, '9'));
    const char *roles[] = {"root", "low", "high", "sum"};
    std::print("| actual call | role | depth | left digits | right digits | split | leaf | result digits " "|\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: |\n");
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.calls.size(); ++i) {
        const auto &c = t.calls[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i,
                   roles[int(c.role)], c.depth, c.left_digits, c.right_digits,
                   c.split, c.leaf, c.product_digits);
        const double x = i ? 5. * (double(i) - 2) : 0, y = i ? 5 : 0;
        d.node(std::to_string(i), {x, y},
               std::format("{}: {} x {}\n{}", roles[int(c.role)], c.left_digits,
                           c.right_digits, c.leaf ? "schoolbook" : "split"));
        if (i)
            d.edge(std::to_string(c.parent), std::to_string(i));
    }
    std::print("\nActual digit products {}; full schoolbook formula33*33={}.\n",
               t.work.digit_products, 33 * 33);
    d.save_svg("build/karatsuba_split.svg");
}
```
