> Derive the three-product identity

Write x=x1 B+x0 and y=y1 B+y0, with B=10^m. Compute z0=x0 y0, z2=x1 y1 and
zsum=(x0+x1)(y0+y1). Then

$$
xy=z_2B^2+(z_{sum}-z_2-z_0)B+z_0.
$$
\alttext(The middle coefficient is the product of half sums minus the two direct half-products, so only three recursive products are required.)

The subtracted middle term is nonnegative because it equals x0 y1+x1 y0. For
balanced large operands, the three half-size calls plus linear digit additions
give the familiar exponent log2(3). Actual crossover, carry growth, unequal
lengths and temporary copies affect a concrete run. This kernel splits at half
the smaller vector width, so balanced-rate intuition should not be substituted
for measurements on severely unequal operands.

> Retain the original constants and reveal their actual base case

The original strings are31 digits from pi and e. Both are below crossover32, so
their native invocation is a schoolbook leaf. Commutativity and identity are
useful controls but are not independent multiplication oracles. Independent
batch checks additionally verified exact products with Python integers.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/karatsuba_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/karatsuba.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <limits>
#include <cmath>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const std::string x =
        "3141592653589793238462643383279", y =
        "2718281828459045235360287471352";
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::karatsuba_trace(x, y);
    std::print("Original left: {}\n\nOriginal right: {}\n\nActual product: {}\n\n",
               x, y, t.product);
    std::print("| left digits | right digits | result digits | actual calls | actual leaves | digit " "products |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
               x.size(), y.size(), t.product.size(), t.work.recursive_calls,
               t.work.schoolbook_leaves, t.work.digit_products);
    if (t.product != dm::algorithms::karatsuba_multiply(y, x) ||
        x != dm::algorithms::karatsuba_multiply(x, "1") ||
        t.calls.size() != 1 || !t.calls[0].leaf)
        throw std::runtime_error("original controls");
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("call", {0, 0},
           std::format("Original {} x {} digits\nActual schoolbook leaf\n{} digit products",
                       x.size(), y.size(), t.work.digit_products)).save_svg(
        "build/karatsuba_original.svg");
}
